    <h2>Converting Midjourney WebP Exports to Lossless PNG and Clean JPEG</h2>
    <p>
      Midjourney web gallery downloads frequently save images in Google's WebP container format. While WebP achieves compact file weights, many legacy creative desktop applications (older Adobe Illustrator versions, Windows Photo Viewer, and certain video editors) refuse to import WebP files.
    </p>
    <p>
      RemoveSynth incorporates multi-format decoding: drop any Midjourney WebP file into our tool, choose your aspect ratio, and select <strong>PNG (Lossless High Quality)</strong> or <strong>JPG (Compact 94%)</strong> in the export selector. The canvas synthesizes a pristine output file instantly with zero external conversion software required.
    </p>

    <h2>Preserving High Resolution: 4K and 8K Scaling in Local Browser RAM</h2>
    <p>
      When working with upscale outputs from Topaz Gigapixel, Magnific AI, or Midjourney upscale buttons (2048px or 4096px), online converters frequently downscale your images to conserve server bandwidth.
    </p>
    <p>
      RemoveSynth uses client-side hardware-accelerated OffscreenCanvas. Your computer or smartphone's GPU renders high-resolution pixel matrices directly in device memory, supporting ultra-high-definition exports up to 8K resolution without watermarks, subscriptions, or compression penalties.
    </p>

    <h2>How to Resize AI Art Without Cropping in 3 Simple Steps</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Select Your Artwork:</strong> Click the upload box above or drag and drop any Midjourney, DALL-E, Gemini, or Stable Diffusion image.</li>
      <li><strong>Choose Aspect Ratio &amp; Background:</strong> Click 16:9, 9:16, 4:5, or 1:1, and select your preferred background extension style (Smart Blur, Solid Black, or Solid White).</li>
      <li><strong>Download Clean Artwork:</strong> Select PNG or JPG and click &quot;Download Resized Artwork&quot; to export your ready-to-publish graphic in milliseconds.</li>
